# mono.xrs - the mono screen (stereo rung 1) reaches BOTH eyes.
#
# The gate that makes per-eye captures trustworthy again (docs/VERIFICATION.md,
# section 2, defect 1): the game frame on the head-locked quad must composite
# non-black in the left eye AND the right eye, with the same bounding box in
# both. A black left eye here is attributed by the sim's own log line
# (`xrsim: eye L composited BLACK ... COMPOSITOR fault` or `... APP fault`).
#
# Foreground the game window first: an unfocused window stops rendering the
# world and a capture then shows HUD on black.
reset
@mod stereo mono
@frames 60
@assert sessionState eq FOCUSED
@assert layersLastFrame ge 1
@assert quadLayers ge 1
@shot mono
@assert capNonBlackL ge 50
@assert capNonBlackR ge 50
